WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.936
- We need to adjust our
mentality for ourselves

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:04.470
and our leaders.

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:07.907 align:start size:97% position:3%
Like, you know, it's been
this way for most of my life,

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:10.643
where the right, when it comes
to something like a boycott,

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:14.480 align:start size:84% position:16%
it was the norm, Dave,
it was mainstream.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.849
Not just from politicians,
from pundits to say things,

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:18.651 align:start size:97% position:3%
like, "Well, we don't do
that, that's not who we are.

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:20.653
Well, that's not who we are."

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:22.688
And then we woke up one day,

00:00:22.688 --> 00:00:24.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Target's telling
your 13-year-old daughter

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:27.360
to chop her boobs off, and
we were shocked at that.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.861
Well, why were we
shocked at that?

00:00:28.861 --> 00:00:30.830
The corporate boardroom was
only ever getting pressure

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.232
from one direction.

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:34.100
The right has to understand now

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.537 align:start size:84% position:16%
that this whole
philosophy of bragging

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:39.506 align:start size:84% position:16%
about not using
power is ridiculous.

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:41.741 align:start size:97% position:3%
If you have the
governorship, like DeSantis,

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.376
you use it like DeSantis.

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:46.646
If you have numbers in
your local community,

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:48.581
you go take over
your school board,

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you make sure your
values are in your school.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.485
You use power.

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:54.220
The communist is
still a minority,

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.389
but he understands
how to use power.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:59.325
We will drive by the local
public library 1,000 times,

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:00.893
you, me, everybody, and
you won't even look at it

00:01:00.893 --> 00:01:02.361
unless you have kids.

00:01:02.361 --> 00:01:03.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a public library,
who gives a crap about it.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.431
The communist drives
by the public library,

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:08.300 align:start size:97% position:3%
and he sees an
opportunity, he sees power.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.637
Why are there child
drag shows going on

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:12.204
at your local public library?

00:01:12.204 --> 00:01:14.174
Because you drove
by it 1,000 times,

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:15.441
and never thought about it,

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:17.177
and he drove by it
and he saw power.

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:19.812
That's why we must
adjust our mentality.

00:01:19.812 --> 00:01:22.482
(gentle music)

00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:28.654 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I'm Dave Rubin,
and joining me today

00:01:28.654 --> 00:01:31.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the author of "The
Anti-Communist Manifesto,"

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:35.461
as well as the host of
"The Jesse Kelly Show."

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:38.164
Jesse Kelly, welcome
to "The Rubin Report."

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:40.567
- Dave, it is an honor to be
here once again, my friend,

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:41.768
as always, Dave.

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:44.404 align:start size:88% position:13%
Yes, I'm a world-famous
author now, Dave.

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:45.872
I'm a very important person now.

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:48.074 align:start size:84% position:16%
- (laughing) Is this
your first book?

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:52.245 align:start size:97% position:3%
- It is my first book, and
will probably be my only book.

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:55.281 align:start size:84% position:16%
The truth is I
don't like to write.

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:58.551 align:start size:97% position:3%
I enjoy doing TV and radio,
that's what I do for a living.

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:00.486
But I don't enjoy writing.

00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:03.489
I just, they were hounding
me, hounding me, hounding me,

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:05.425
"Hey, we want you to write
a book," for a few years.

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:07.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I always just said,
"No," I wasn't interested.

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:08.928
And then they said, "What
if you wrote something

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:10.329
about anti-communism,"

00:02:10.329 --> 00:02:12.231
'cause that's what I'm
most passionate about.

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:14.700
And I said, "Yes,
that I will write."

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:19.505 align:start position:0%
So this is my one-off
probably, but I am proud of it.

00:02:19.505 --> 00:02:22.408
- Before we get into the
specifics of the book,

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:24.911
and the political machinations,

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:26.980 align:start size:81% position:19%
and all of the
lunacy of the day,

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.848
I wanna talk about your height,

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:31.984
because you're like
8'7" or something.

00:02:31.984 --> 00:02:33.920 align:start size:84% position:16%
And every time I see
you in real life,

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.187
despite the fact
that I've seen you,

00:02:35.187 --> 00:02:37.590
I don't know, probably a
dozen times in reality,

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.425
because you're in a
small box right now,

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:43.262 align:start size:97% position:3%
you seem normal size, but
in real, you're 6'8", right?

00:02:43.262 --> 00:02:44.797
Like, you're huge, man.

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:46.298
You should be in the NBA,

00:02:46.298 --> 00:02:48.368 align:start size:88% position:13%
and instead you're
babbling about politics

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:49.802
with schmucks like me.

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:52.105
- Okay, hold on, yes, I'm 6'8",

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:53.940
but I'm also unathletic, Dave.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:57.610
I'm slow, I can't jump,
I'm not coordinated.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:58.878
So those things always-

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:00.180 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Have you thought
about the WNBA?

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:03.082
- (laughing) They put a ceiling

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:05.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
on my athletic
achievements, that's one.

00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:07.953
Two, you think I'm tall,

00:03:07.953 --> 00:03:09.222
and that hits you
when you meet me,

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:10.456
and I always get
this from people,

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:11.757
"Oh, I can't believe
I'll tall you are,

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:13.026
I didn't realize that."

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:14.561
You know, what hits me, Dave?

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:18.598
How short everyone else
is that I see on TV,

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:19.966 align:start size:84% position:16%
or something like
that, when you meet,

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:21.734
because everyone on
TV, in my opinion,

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.603
looks like they're a good size.

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:25.438 align:start size:84% position:16%
He takes up the
whole screen, right?

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:27.240
So you think, now, by
the way, Dave Rubin,

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.642
for those who've never met
him, is tall, I would guess

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:31.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're at least six feet.
- Thank you.

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:34.713
- But so many people I meet
are just minuscule, Dave.

00:03:34.713 --> 00:03:36.115 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'll walk up to
them, and I'm used to

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:37.783 align:start size:84% position:16%
this larger-than-life
personality,

00:03:37.783 --> 00:03:39.252 align:start size:88% position:13%
and I feel like patting
him on the head,

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:41.254
and getting him a
binky or something.

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:45.391
- (laughing) All right,
well, beyond your height,

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.326
one of the reasons I
love doing your show,

00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:48.528
and that, you know,

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:49.462 align:start size:88% position:13%
we're kinda in the same
circles these days,

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:50.696
is 'cause I think we both have

00:03:50.696 --> 00:03:52.798 align:start size:81% position:19%
a similar attitude
about politics.

00:03:52.798 --> 00:03:55.268 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's like we talk
about politics, we're
passionate about it,

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:57.003 align:start size:84% position:16%
but we're also
trying to have fun.

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:59.539
We're trying to make
our audience laugh,
and not, you know,

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:01.340
so many people are just
riling these people up,

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.075
and then sending them
out into the world.

00:04:03.075 --> 00:04:05.144 align:start size:84% position:16%
When did you get
involved in politics,

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:06.379
or interested in politics,

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:09.781
or any version of like
what that was about you

00:04:09.781 --> 00:04:12.518 align:start size:97% position:3%
that made you wanna do this
the way that you do it?

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:15.521 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Pretty late in life, which
probably explains a lot,

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:17.490 align:start size:88% position:13%
including what you were
just talking about,

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.993
I always loved history,
I was always a reader.

00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:21.194
Now I was a very bad student,

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:23.629
I got a 0.0 in my first
semester of college,

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:25.731
that's real by the way,
I was a very bad student,

00:04:25.731 --> 00:04:27.066 align:start size:97% position:3%
but I-
- How, wait, is that possible?

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:28.368
How's that even possible?

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:30.836 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Well Dave, there's
beer, and there's girls,

00:04:30.836 --> 00:04:32.905
and as long as there's
plenty of that around,

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:34.473
you don't ever end up in class,

00:04:34.473 --> 00:04:36.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
I figured out, if no one's
there to make you go.

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:38.911
So it was a very fun semester,

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:40.880 align:start size:97% position:3%
but not the most productive
one in the world.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.382 align:start size:97% position:3%
Anyway, but I didn't get
political until late in life.

00:04:43.382 --> 00:04:46.319
I grew up in a construction
family, that's my background.

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:48.421 align:start size:88% position:13%
Joined the Marines,
got out of the Marines,

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:49.888
started going to
community college,

00:04:49.888 --> 00:04:52.425 align:start position:0%
right back to construction,
that's just what I was gonna do.

00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:54.093
And then Obama ran for office,

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:55.827 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I ended up
running for Congress,

00:04:55.827 --> 00:04:58.131
'cause I was so mad about
him running for office

00:04:58.131 --> 00:05:00.266
a couple times in Arizona.

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:01.767
Ended up staying in the fight,

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:04.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
going back to the private
sector, selling RVs.

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:06.238 align:start size:88% position:13%
So I've only been
doing like TV and radio

00:05:06.238 --> 00:05:08.140
four or five years.

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:10.209
But you're right, I'm
on the same philosophy.

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:11.778
I mean, I did it
in the book too.

00:05:11.778 --> 00:05:13.012
I do it on my radio show.

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:15.147 align:start size:84% position:16%
I do it on my TV show,
just like you do.

00:05:15.147 --> 00:05:17.450
I don't like to scream
and yell all day long.

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:19.451 align:start size:81% position:19%
There's enough bad
news out there.

00:05:19.451 --> 00:05:20.987
And we talk about
that very frankly,

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:22.554
but screaming and yelling,

00:05:22.554 --> 00:05:24.223
and my blood pressure's
going through the roof,

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:25.958
that I'm upset and you're upset.

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:28.194 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then that's just,
there's way too much of that.

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:29.528
I don't like it.

00:05:29.528 --> 00:05:32.130
- What was it that you
saw about Obama early on

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:34.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
that probably, I suppose,
led to a guy like you

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:36.735
writing a book like this?

00:05:36.735 --> 00:05:40.840 align:start position:0%
- Well, again, I wasn't, I
always knew we were Republican,

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:43.142 align:start size:97% position:3%
but that was one
conversation with my parents.

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:44.610
I think I was in kindergarten.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.345 align:start size:88% position:13%
"Hey Dad, are we
Democrat or Republican?"

00:05:46.345 --> 00:05:47.547
"We're Republican."

00:05:47.547 --> 00:05:48.648 align:start size:84% position:16%
I didn't even know
why, just, "Oh, okay."

00:05:48.648 --> 00:05:51.918
So it wasn't a political house,

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:53.885
but it was a patriotic house.

00:05:53.885 --> 00:05:56.688
And I mentioned that I
was reading all the time.

00:05:56.688 --> 00:06:00.126 align:start size:97% position:3%
I was a geek for military
history, and military fiction,

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:01.793 align:start size:84% position:16%
and military anything
when I was a kid,

00:06:01.793 --> 00:06:04.396
just gimme a book on the
Marines and let me read it.

00:06:04.396 --> 00:06:06.232
So I really was raised

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:08.701 align:start size:84% position:16%
with a deep, deep
love of the country.

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:12.171 align:start size:97% position:3%
And while I never really
cared honestly about Clinton,

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:14.807
and a lot of these guys, I
knew all the controversies.

00:06:14.807 --> 00:06:17.710
Obama was the first guy I
saw running for president

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:21.346
that I really, I could tell
he really hates the country.

00:06:21.346 --> 00:06:23.416
He really, really
hated the country.

00:06:23.416 --> 00:06:25.651
And I was so aghast
at the thought of,

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:28.620
'cause I guess I probably had
lofty ideals back then, Dave.

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:31.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was a little less jaded
about the presidency,

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.525
and who the president should be,

00:06:32.525 --> 00:06:35.027
and the statesman who
should lead America.

00:06:35.027 --> 00:06:36.762
And I just was horrified

00:06:36.762 --> 00:06:39.498
that someone who hated
the place might lead it.

00:06:39.498 --> 00:06:41.401 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that's, from
there I just remember

00:06:41.401 --> 00:06:43.469 align:start size:88% position:13%
marching down to the
local Republican office.

00:06:43.469 --> 00:06:45.238 align:start size:84% position:16%
I didn't even know
how to run for office.

00:06:45.238 --> 00:06:46.506 align:start size:84% position:16%
I said, "I'm running
for something."

00:06:46.506 --> 00:06:48.407
(laughing) That's how it went.

00:06:48.407 --> 00:06:50.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
- (laughing) They said,
"We'll take that 6'8" guy,

00:06:50.943 --> 00:06:53.346
and see if he can run,
let's see what happens.

00:06:53.346 --> 00:06:54.613 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yeah, well it-
- You know, it's funny,

00:06:54.613 --> 00:06:56.582 align:start size:84% position:16%
'cause I know you know
my story obviously,

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:57.817
about coming from the left.

00:06:57.817 --> 00:06:59.418
And I was on board
the Obama thing,

00:06:59.418 --> 00:07:00.820
and I voted for him twice.

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:04.156 align:start size:84% position:16%
But I remember day
one of his presidency,

00:07:04.156 --> 00:07:06.658 align:start size:84% position:16%
when Michelle Obama
said that thing about,

00:07:06.658 --> 00:07:09.495
"This is the first day I've
ever been proud of America."

00:07:09.495 --> 00:07:11.030
I remember suddenly being like,

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:13.532
"Whoa, what, whoa, what, huh?

00:07:13.532 --> 00:07:14.900 align:start size:84% position:16%
How'd that happen?"
- Yeah.

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:17.036
It bothered me so much.

00:07:17.036 --> 00:07:20.205
It made me political,
because like I said,

00:07:20.205 --> 00:07:22.575 align:start size:84% position:16%
I wasn't even
active in politics.

00:07:22.575 --> 00:07:23.943
I wasn't doing any of that.

00:07:23.943 --> 00:07:25.844
I was working construction,

00:07:25.844 --> 00:07:28.413
I just met my wife, so
I'm chasing all my money.

00:07:28.413 --> 00:07:30.482
I'm spending all my money
chasing her around, Dave.

00:07:30.482 --> 00:07:31.750
You know how it goes.

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:33.886
And I just wasn't,
I wasn't involved,

00:07:33.886 --> 00:07:35.754 align:start size:84% position:16%
but the more I read
about this guy,

00:07:35.754 --> 00:07:38.657 align:start position:0%
I thought to myself, "Wait,
this guy's gonna be the nominee?

00:07:38.657 --> 00:07:40.660
What? This guy can't
be the president."

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:42.828
And look, the rest is history.

00:07:42.828 --> 00:07:44.363
- So since the book is called

00:07:44.363 --> 00:07:46.432
"The Anti-Communist Manifesto,"

00:07:46.432 --> 00:07:47.800
and I'm sure many
people are familiar

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:50.035
with "The Communist Manifesto,"

00:07:50.035 --> 00:07:53.472
first off, do you make a
distinction at this point,

00:07:53.472 --> 00:07:55.107
is there an important
distinction to make

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:58.444
between socialist, communist,

00:07:58.444 --> 00:08:00.279
and even Democrat at this point?

00:08:00.279 --> 00:08:01.781 align:start size:81% position:19%
Like how would you
sort of line up

00:08:01.781 --> 00:08:04.283
each one of those ideologies?

00:08:04.283 --> 00:08:05.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah, there's no
difference in any of them.

00:08:05.885 --> 00:08:07.352
So there's no need,
there's no point

00:08:07.352 --> 00:08:09.188 align:start size:84% position:16%
in making any
distinctions at all.

00:08:09.188 --> 00:08:10.689
Because this is what we do,

00:08:10.689 --> 00:08:13.826 align:start size:97% position:3%
and this is actually what
they do very, very well to us,

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:15.060
and then we oblige.

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:18.797 align:start size:88% position:13%
We stress because you
have a moral code, Dave.

00:08:18.797 --> 00:08:20.967 align:start size:88% position:13%
Now I don't have much
of one, but I have some.

00:08:20.967 --> 00:08:22.968 align:start size:84% position:16%
(Dave laughing)
But because of that,

00:08:22.968 --> 00:08:24.737
there are things
we don't wanna be,

00:08:24.737 --> 00:08:26.005
and things we don't wanna do.

00:08:26.005 --> 00:08:29.041
Like, I don't want to be
a hypocrite or a liar.

00:08:29.041 --> 00:08:30.576 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm a bad person,
but I don't wanna be

